            "properties": {
                "0": {
                    "name": "block",
                    "value": "Lists the different values that occur, in order, with how many times each occurs and, for every element, which of them it is. Which labels were seen, how often each gesture class appeared, which performers (by id) are present.\n\nSYNTAX:\nt.unique\n\nINPUTS and PARAMETERS:\n\ntensor in:\nThe values. Every input sends.\n\nOUTPUTS:\n\nvalues:\nThe different values, smallest first.\n\ncounts:\nHow many times each occurs. Sent second.\n\ninverse:\nFor every element of the input, the position in values of its value - the input rewritten as numbers 0, 1, 2 ... Sent first.\n\nThe answer stays on the input's device: a tensor on the GPU is worked on there and comes out there.\n\nREADING THE DEMO:\n3 1 3 2 1 3 has three different values, 1 2 3, occurring 2, 1 and 3 times. The input rewritten: 3 is value 2, 1 is value 0, and so on.\n\nRELATED:\nnp.unique is the numpy version. t.mode gives the most common value. t.bincount counts whole numbers 0, 1, 2 ...",
                    "value_type": "str"
                },
                "1": {
                    "name": "lock",
                    "value": true,
                    "value_type": "bool"
                },
                "2": {
                    "name": "width",
                    "value": 760,
                    "value_type": "int"
                },
                "3": {
                    "name": "height",
                    "value": 950,
                    "value_type": "int"
                },
                "4": {
                    "name": "text_size",
                    "value": "30",
                    "value_type": "str"
                }
            },
            "text": "Lists the different values that occur, in order, with how many times each occurs and, for every element, which of them it is. Which labels were seen, how often each gesture class appeared, which performers (by id) are present.\n\nSYNTAX:\nt.unique\n\nINPUTS and PARAMETERS:\n\ntensor in:\nThe values. Every input sends.\n\nOUTPUTS:\n\nvalues:\nThe different values, smallest first.\n\ncounts:\nHow many times each occurs. Sent second.\n\ninverse:\nFor every element of the input, the position in values of its value - the input rewritten as numbers 0, 1, 2 ... Sent first.\n\nThe answer stays on the input's device: a tensor on the GPU is worked on there and comes out there.\n\nREADING THE DEMO:\n3 1 3 2 1 3 has three different values, 1 2 3, occurring 2, 1 and 3 times. The input rewritten: 3 is value 2, 1 is value 0, and so on.\n\nRELATED:\nnp.unique is the numpy version. t.mode gives the most common value. t.bincount counts whole numbers 0, 1, 2 ..."
        },
